# Flaky-test policy

Scaffolded by {{generated_by}} on {{date}}. Owner of this policy: TODO (the team that owns the merge gate).

A test is **flaky** when it both passes and fails on the same code. A flaky test is a bug in the
test or in the product; a retry that turns it green hides the bug. Quarantine is a stopgap with an
owner and an expiry date, never a fix.

## 1. Detect

- Repeat the suspect tests with shuffling and recorded seeds where the runner supports it:
  `node <skill>/scripts/adc.mjs flake-probe --tests "<id>" --times 20 --json` (pytest-randomly +
  pytest-repeat, `go test -count=10 -shuffle=on`, `jest --randomize`, `cargo nextest run --retries 0`,
  a `dotnet test` loop; otherwise N sequential runs, recorded as `shuffle: false`).
- Compare pass/fail across runs; keep the failing seeds, they reproduce the order.
- Detected runner: **{{runner_name}}**; e2e runner: **{{e2e_runner}}**.

## 2. Classify (one class per incident)

| Class | Typical signal | Fix pattern |
|---|---|---|
| Order dependence | fails only in some orders or seeds; passes alone | isolate state per test, reset globals, deterministic seeds |
| Time and timezone | fails near midnight, at DST changes, in another TZ | fake timers (`jest.useFakeTimers`, `vi.useFakeTimers`, Playwright `page.clock`, freezegun, time-machine) |
| Network | timeouts, DNS errors, third-party 5xx | mock at the boundary (MSW 3 `onUnhandledFrame: 'error'`, nock `disableNetConnect`, respx, VCR.py / pytest-recording `--block-network`, WireMock) |
| Concurrency | races between parallel workers or async steps | wait on conditions, never sleep; one resource per worker |
| Resource leaks | later tests fail; open handles | explicit cleanup in fixtures; `--detectOpenHandles`; pytest-timeout |
| Test-data collisions | unique-constraint errors, shared accounts | unique data per test or worker; factories instead of shared fixtures |
| Environment | Windows paths, line endings, locale, CPU speed | `path.join`, normalize EOL, pin locale and TZ, no timing thresholds |

## 3. Quarantine (stopgap)

1. Tag the test `@quarantine` (name or tag). With {{runner_name}}: `{{quarantine_only}}` selects
   quarantined tests and `{{quarantine_skip}}` excludes them.
2. Add an entry to `{{registry}}`: `id`, `owner`, `issue`, `added`, `expires` (at most 30 days
   later), `reason`.
3. The merge gate excludes quarantined tests (`scaffold ci-gate` adds the exclusion and a registry
   check when `{{registry}}` exists). The weekly `quarantine` workflow runs them with retries off
   and fails on expired or incomplete entries.
4. Weekly review: fix the test, extend once with a written reason, or delete it.

## 4. Retries

- Allowed only for e2e tests and only with a flaky report, so a retried pass is visible and fails
  the run: Playwright `failOnFlakyTests` / `--fail-on-flaky-tests`, Surefire `Flakes:` with
  `rerunFailingTestsCount`, Vitest `retry` with the flaky outcome in JUnit. Never for unit tests.
- CI fails when more than {{max_flaky}} flaky test(s) are reported (`ci-gate --max-flaky`).
- `gh run rerun --failed` hides flakes: a green re-run is not evidence.
- In-source retries (`jest.retryTimes`, `@pytest.mark.flaky`, `describe.configure({ retries })`)
  are findings in `verify` (CK-RETRY).

## 5. Evidence

Every quarantine and every fix carries the flake-probe evidence (command, runs, seeds, failures)
in the PR description, and the fix is verified by a second probe with zero failures.

@@@ file: .github/workflows/quarantine.yml scope=repo @@@
{{header}}
# Weekly review of quarantined tests (not part of the merge gate): every registry entry needs an
# owner, an issue and an unexpired date, and the quarantined tests run with retries off so fixed
# tests can leave the quarantine. Edit freely: a later `verify` reports weakening edits as findings.
name: quarantine

on:
  schedule:
    - cron: '23 6 * * 1'
  pull_request:
    paths:
      - {{registry}}
  workflow_dispatch:

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:
  registry:
    name: Quarantine registry
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 5
    outputs:
      count: ${{ steps.check.outputs.count }}
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v7
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v7
        with:
          node-version: 24
      - name: Owners, issues and expiry dates
        id: check
        run: |
          node .github/adc/gate.mjs quarantine --registry {{registry}}

  quarantined-tests:
    name: Quarantined tests, retries off
    needs: registry
    if: ${{ needs.registry.outputs.count != '0' }}
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 45
    defaults:
      run:
        shell: bash
        working-directory: {{project_root}}
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v7
{{setup}}
      - name: Install (frozen)
        run: |
          {{install_cmd}}
      - name: Run only the quarantined tests ({{runner_name}})
        run: |
          {{quarantine_run}}

